| H7 | `DECISIONS.md` byte-identical to `MIGRATION_BASELINE`, proven by `git diff --quiet` exit status and an independent length/hash equality — commission §2.2 hard stop | `PASS` — `git diff --quiet` exited `0`; both copies are `76314` bytes with SHA-256 `b22b3fffc058a5e84931ca1b14b08a1b7f1206d1ccd5154a7a7f1de8ad0f0d6e` |
| H8 | Amendment 4 committed on `main` before creation of `codex/decisions-migration` — chronology disposition `PASS` / `FAIL` / `UNPROVEN` | `PASS` — `main` reached `05f9bcdddf9ce92f80bcd05fb5c4c5399fd466d5` at `2026-07-29 11:57:20 -0400`; the branch was created from that commit at `2026-07-29 12:21:42 -0400`; `main` preceded branch creation by `24 minutes 22 seconds` |
| H9 | Frozen phase-1 artifacts and the pre-migration graph unchanged — commission §2.1 item 7 | `PASS` — all six prescribed paths are byte-identical to `05f9bcdddf9ce92f80bcd05fb5c4c5399fd466d5`; the cleanup directory contains exactly its five prescribed files; unexpected members: none |

**Recorded here because the manifest must not launder it.** Commission §2.1 item 2 requires the Amendment 4
text to be applied to the taxonomy, format specification, and fixture file **and committed on `main` before
the migration branch is created**. M0.2 shows all three were applied by `05f9bcd`, which M0.1 records as the
current HEAD of `codex/decisions-migration`.

H8 is a **chronology** proof, not a containment check. Membership of `05f9bcd` in `main` today does not
establish that `main` reached it before the branch was created, and only the ordering satisfies the
precondition as ratified. H8 therefore proves three limbs independently — containment, the `main` reflog
arrival, and the branch-creation reflog entry — and returns `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `UNPROVEN`. Absent reflog
evidence is `UNPROVEN`, never an inferred pass.

**A non-pass requires compliant remediation or an amendment to the commission.** It is not merely an owner
call, and it cannot be waived by declaration: the precondition is ratified text, and a ratified precondition
is discharged by satisfying it or by amending it under Principle 27, never by asserting it was probably met.
H8 establishes the fact and disposes of nothing. Neither this seat nor Codex may resolve it.

