## M1. Authority and scope of this manifest

This manifest is the sole authority for every byte Stage 2b writes into target `DECISIONS.md` and the
normalized migration archive. **No target text may be inferred, paraphrased, completed, shortened, retitled,
redated, or omitted outside this manifest.** Where this manifest is silent, Stage 2b stops and returns to
the architect seat rather than making the obvious choice.

This manifest carries no prose instruction of the form "compress appropriately," "preserve the intent,"
"use the current title," or "include evidence where available." Every target choice is written out as
literal bytes.

Sibling drafts `DECISIONS-MIGRATION-STAGE-2A-PART-A-ARCHITECT-DRAFT-2026-07-29.md` through `PART-D` are
preparatory and are **not** authorities. This manifest inlines their content; no pointer to them survives as
a construction instruction. The manifest scaffold and the live-source packet are likewise preparatory.

Ratification of the commission, of Amendment 4, or of Amendment 1 does not ratify any byte below.
Commission §12 requires a separate owner act on these exact manifest bytes.

