**The four retirement phrases do not move.** The four `retired 2026-07-28` phrases are historical
retirement dates ratified on that day. The nine `archived` phrases carry the archival date and move with a
rebinding. Anchors contain no date-dependent token at all.

### M5.7 The six-row retired-identifier register

```markdown
Retired and never-assigned identifiers are permanently unavailable. This register is append-only; an
entry never leaves it, and no live entry may carry a listed identifier.

| ID | disposition | date | pointer |
|---|---|---|---|
| P9 | RETIRED | 2026-07-28 | `Archive/DECISIONS-ARCHIVE-2026-08-11.md#p9-the-case-skeleton-is-english-only` |
| P12 | RETIRED | 2026-07-28 | `Archive/DECISIONS-ARCHIVE-2026-08-11.md#p12-author-side-currency-via-closed-world-construction-and-routed-flags` |
| P13 | NEVER ASSIGNED | — | — |
| P14 | NEVER ASSIGNED | — | — |
| P18 | RETIRED | 2026-07-28 | `Archive/DECISIONS-ARCHIVE-2026-08-11.md#p18-fact-check-and-flag-only-review-are-chain-steps` |
| P22 | RETIRED | 2026-07-28 | `Archive/DECISIONS-ARCHIVE-2026-08-11.md#p22-opus-skeleton-cases-are-gpt-provenance-for-review-conflict-purposes` |
```

The four register dates are retirement dates and do not move. Only the pointer filenames move.

Parse notes. The register parser locates the header row inside target §8 and skips exactly one separator
line, so the separator must be the single `|---|---|---|---|` row shown. `RETIRED` rows require both a
`YYYY-MM-DD` date and a backticked pointer; `NEVER ASSIGNED` rows require both cells to be exactly `—`.
Register order is ascending numeric, which the parser does not require but which matches the format
specification's worked example. Neither introductory sentence opens `- **`, so neither can be captured as
an archive-index line.

### M5.8 Parse and conformance verification for M5

Verified against `lib/decisions-format.ts`:

- Each label line matches `^- \*\*(.+)\*\* — .+$`; no label contains `**`, so the greedy capture ends
  at the intended delimiter.
- Each pointer line is exactly two spaces, a backtick, the file path, `#`, the anchor, a backtick. The file
  part contains no `#`, which the pointer regex requires.
- The four ID-addressed labels take the shape `<ID> <title>` with a single space and no em dash, which is
  the `expectedLabel` the conformance check builds from the wrapper heading. The nine name-addressed labels
  equal their wrapper titles byte-for-byte.
- No name-addressed label begins `P<n> ` or `R<n> `, so none parses as ID-addressed and none can fail
  `ARCHIVE_INDEX_MISMATCH` against a name-addressed wrapper.
- Every anchor equals `markdownHeadingAnchor` of its wrapper heading. For the four ID-addressed wrappers the
  anchor is derived from the full `<ID> — <title>` heading, so the em dash collapses into the surrounding
  hyphen run.
- Thirteen labels, thirteen wrappers, bijection by block key. Thirteen distinct headings, thirteen distinct
  labels, thirteen distinct anchors.
- Exactly four wrappers carry `Retired ID`, and the register carries exactly those four plus the two
  never-assigned rows, so the register and the wrapper set agree and no live entry carries a listed
  identifier.

**Qualification, carried forward and not softened.** Nine of these wrappers are name-addressed with
`Original Kind` `P` or `R` — `E032`, `E039b`, and `E075` with `P`, and `E036`, `E048`, `E050`, `E051`,
`E052`, and `E076` with `R`. The parser as it currently sits on disk rejects every one of them with
`INVALID_FIELD_VALUE`, at the single guard Amendment 4 §4.3 delegates to Stage 2b for removal. These nine
are valid under the **ratified post-guard grammar**, not under the current parser. That is by design, and
the fixture pre-failure that must be observed before the guard is removed is commission §5.3 item 2.

**Six historical-metadata calls the reviewer must re-derive rather than accept as a pattern.**
`Original Kind: R` on `E036`, `E048`, `E050`, `E051`, `E052`, and `E076` asserts that material which never
held an `R` number was historically a concrete ruling. That is the truthful reading and it is what
Amendment 4 exists to permit, but it is six separate architect judgments about historical metadata and they
should be checked one at a time. `Original Kind: P` on `E075` is flagged separately at that record.

**Not verified by this seat.** The thirteen source hashes are reproduced from
`DECISIONS-MIGRATION-STAGE-2A-ARCHIVE-SPAN-HASHES-2026-07-29.md` and were not recomputed from `git show`
here; the `E038` slice hash is reproduced from that same file's addendum. Commission §4.9 requires the
independent Stage 2a reviewer to reproduce all fourteen slices and hashes from `MIGRATION_BASELINE`, and
that obligation is undischarged.

