### M6.6 `Authorized`, `Not authorized`, and `Execution` omissions

These three fields sit outside commission §4.6's candidate-resolution procedure — none of them takes a
repository path — but each absence is still an architect decision under §4.4 item 10, and silence is not an
omission. Membership is the `omitted` column of §M6.2; the grounds are classed here.

**`Authorized` — 63 omissions, 2 present.** Present on `R1#0` and `R6#0`. The uniform ground is that the
entry grants no permission beyond what its own statement carries, so a separate line would either duplicate
the statement or manufacture a grant. One record's ground is specific and is stated at its item 10: `R5#0`
keeps its implementation latitude inside the statement because the grant is bounded by three constraints in
the same sentence, and splitting the grant from its bounds across a field boundary would let the grant be
read without them.

**`Not authorized` — 61 omissions, 4 present.** Present on `P5#1`, `P29#0`, `P30#0`, and `R6#0`. The uniform
ground is that the entry withholds no permission beyond what its statement already carries. Four records
carry specific grounds at their item 10 and are the reviewable set here: `R1#0`, whose only negative limb is
a non-relaxation of two existing disciplines that the statement carries directly; `R3#0` and `R5#0`, whose
negative limbs concern vital-sign sides that the target §7 thread carries rather than these entries; and
`R4#0`, whose permanent unavailability of the bootstrap is a live rule the statement carries rather than a
withheld permission. Standing ruling 24 governs the opposite direction — a ruling's closing
non-authorization belongs in this field rather than being compressed away — and `P29#0` and `P30#0` are the
two records where it fired.

**`Execution` — 23 omissions, 42 present.** The dominant ground is that the frozen classification carries no
execution state for the entry, and it is not an architect choice; the classification is an input. Several
records add a second limb at item 10 — that the entry decides nothing implementable, advises rather than
decides, or fixes a standing property rather than a decision that is built or pending. **`Execution` is the
one optional field whose omissions are mostly not discretionary,** and a reviewer should test them against
the frozen classification rather than against this manifest's judgment.

### M6.7 Omissions first grounded at M6

Ten rows carry a ground stated here rather than at the record. Eight of them are `NO-CANDIDATE` on
`Evidence`, which asserts only that no candidate was proposed at the record or in any draft register — a
negative that is checkable by search rather than a claim that no eligible source could exist. **This is new
architect text and must be reviewed as such**, not read as a transcription of an existing decision.

The population grew from eight to ten on 2026-08-04. `P4#0` and `P7#0` were added: their draft registers
recorded a **joint** `Evidence, Owner` row under a single reason, and that reason is Owner-shaped, so it
discharges the `Owner` omission and not the `Evidence` one. A joint row carrying one field-shaped reason is
the field-test collapse at its source, not an inheritance.

| register row | record | block | field | ground | note |
|---:|---|---|---|---|---|
| 13 | M4.8 | `P5#1` | Owner | `NO-EXECUTABLE-OWNER` | The entry generalizes a constitutional floor to named-model policy under standing ruling 10; `P31` separately carries the current model-specific restrictions. Neither is a rule a path executes. |
| 22 | M4.13 | `P11#0` | Evidence | `NO-CANDIDATE` | Part A registered the `Owner` candidate only. No `Evidence` candidate was proposed at the record or in Part A §4. |
| 27 | M4.16 | `P16#0` | Evidence | `NO-CANDIDATE` | Part A registered the `Owner` candidate only. The ratifying evidence base recorded at `P16#1` belongs to that attachment, not to this core. |
| 32 | M4.19 | `P17#0` | Evidence | `NO-CANDIDATE` | Part A registered the `Owner` candidate only. |
| 34 | M4.20 | `P19#0` | Evidence | `NO-CANDIDATE` | Part B registered the `Owner` candidate only. The statement's census exclusion is carried by ratification, and no tracked source was proposed as its evidence. |
| 36 | M4.21 | `P20#0` | Evidence | `NO-CANDIDATE` | Part B registered the `Owner` candidates only. |
