**Why the `Owner` ground was not copied across.** Standing ruling 23 fixes that `Evidence` and `Owner` have
different tests, so a recorded `Owner` ground is not evidence for the `Evidence` omission on the same
record. Three records — `P3#0`, `P10#0`, and `P16#2` — also carried a bare `Evidence — OMIT` at item 10 and
are **not** flagged here. `P16#2`'s draft reason is expressly applicable to both fields; `P3#0` and `P10#0`
have their item-10 `Evidence` reasoning repaired under the 2026-08-04 work order, so their grounds are
stated at the record rather than only here.

